\f2\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 <!$Scr_H::3>
\f0 It creates an attractive escalation:\
UDF arrives 
\f3 \uc0\u8594 
\f0  Shakti humiliates UDF 
\f3 \uc0\u8594 
\f0  Elvi arrive 
\f3 \uc0\u8594 
\f0  golf 
\f3 \uc0\u8594 
\f0  commerce 
\f3 \uc0\u8594 
\f0  Airborne kids 
\f3 \uc0\u8594 
\f0  mansions 
\f3 \uc0\u8594 
\f0  pubs 
\f3 \uc0\u8594 
\f0  soldiers join the fun.\
That escalation is 
\f1\b \strokec2 too satisfying
\f0\b0 \strokec2 .\
It tells the reader, subconsciously, that this is what happened next. The environment develops in a clean causal sequence and arrives at a mature state.\
Then the book would have to say, effectively:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f4\i \cf0 Meanwhile, earlier that morning, a hover-copt crashed.
\f0\i0 \

\f4\i Meanwhile, before those soldiers were at the pub, Alexander arrived.
\f0\i0 \

\f4\i Meanwhile, while the pubs and mansions were filling, Johnny was restarting Kebab.
\f0\i0 \
